# >>> AI WORKFLOW MANAGED >>>
# Installed by ai-dev-workflow-template install.sh — keeps the workflow
# footprint out of this project's git history.
.ai/
.claude/
.agents/
# <<< AI WORKFLOW MANAGED <<<

# Two files under .claude/ are NucleOS, not the workflow footprint the block above excludes.
# core/src/autopilot.rs reads settings.json and refuses to activate autopilot unless it registers
# ask_daemon.py and that script is present on disk — the PreToolUse hook is the single point where
# the safety gate meets a running tool. Excluding them made them tracked-but-uncommittable:
# editable forever, and a fix to the security hook could never land.
#
# Deliberately below the managed block so the template's installer can rewrite its own lines
# without taking these with it. The directory has to be re-included before a file inside it can be:
# git never descends into an excluded directory, so `!.claude/settings.json` alone does nothing.
!.claude/
.claude/*
!.claude/settings.json
!.claude/hooks/
.claude/hooks/*
!.claude/hooks/ask_daemon.py

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Rust + Tauri + Node build artifacts
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/target/
/shell/node_modules/
/shell/dist/
/shell/src-tauri/target/
*.db
*.db-journal
sidecars/**/*.exe

# TypeScript incremental-build artifacts (emitted by `tsc -b`)
*.tsbuildinfo
/shell/vite.config.js
/shell/vite.config.d.ts

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Agent instruction files — local only, never committed
# (patterns without a leading slash match at every depth)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md

# Local git hooks (core.hooksPath) — local only, never committed.
# A rule rather than a habit: without this the directory is merely untracked, one `git add -A`
# away from entering history. Recreate it with scripts/install-hooks.sh.
.githooks/
